  "name": "Aïssawa (ʿIsawiyya brotherhood hadra)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ritual music of the ʿIsawiyya Sufi order founded in Meknes by the sixteenth-century saint Sidi Muhammad ibn ʿIsa, whose shrine in Meknes hosts the order's annual moussem and whose lodges across Moroccan cities hold hadra ceremonies. Chanted dhikr and praise poetry lead into trance dancing, with ghaita shawms and tbel drums outdoors and bendir and taarija frame and clay drums indoors. Paul Bowles recorded the order in 1959 for the Library of Congress.",
  "recipe": "classic North African late-1950s aïssawa, ritual Devotional, Sufi branch. single lead single track no stacking. ghaita, tbel, juniper bent frame canonical Maghrebi goat skin tacked canonical Sufi bendir, taarija. stone plaster medina room. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
